{"name":"Aru Ressha","hex":"#cca537","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aru","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Arua."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aru"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aru Ressha","blocks":[{"text":"The Aru Ressha (或る列車) is a luxury excursion train operated by Kyushu Railway Company in Japan since 2015. It comprises a two-car diesel-powered railcar heavily modified to parody the style, especially in its window treatment, of passenger cars supplied to Japan by the J. G. Brill Company of Philadelphia, United States of America in 1908."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/JRKyushu_DMU_ARU_RESSHA.jpg/330px-JRKyushu_DMU_ARU_RESSHA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aru_Ressha","wikidata":"Q11370351"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_influenced_the_design_of_the_Aru_Ressha_cars_of_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_influenced_the_design_of_the_Aru_Ressha_cars_of_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_influenced_the_design_of_the_Aru_Ressha_cars_of_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_influenced_the_design_of_the_Aru_Ressha_cars_of_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_influenced_the_design_of_the_Aru_Ressha_cars_of_2015_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Models_of_the_J._G._Brill_Company_passenger_cars_of_1908_that_in